<div id="body" class="mktoText" style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, Sans-Serif; padding:10px;">
<p>Hi {{lead.First Name:default=Friend}},</p> 
<div>
In your industry, the competition is fierce. Your competitors who are tackling their global payment strategy and tying it to their overall Accounts Receivable (A/R) process are winning. 
<br />
<br /> So how can your team get ahead of the competition and retain your customers? Your A/R may be the answer. 
<br />
<br /> Your A/R process touches every existing customer and their renewal. Did you know you're 60-70% likely to sell to an existing customer, compared to the 5-20% likelihood of selling to a new prospect? 
<br />
<br /> After speaking with many customers, our EVP &amp; GM of B2B at Flywire, Ryan Frere, has put together a list of 
<a href="https://www.flywire.com/resources/how-b2b-companies-are-using-accounts-receivable-to-help-grow-their-business?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email" target="_blank" id="">five ways executive teams are thinking about A/R functions as strategic levers of growth.</a>
<br />
<br /> Thank you, 
<br />Alex Godfrey
<br />
</div> 
<div>
